        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is this safe for confidential documents?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "It is structurally safer than any upload-based service, because the file is never written to a disk you do not control. WebRTC data channels are encrypted in transit by default (DTLS), and you can add your own AES-256 password layer on top. There is no account, no log, and nothing to delete afterwards because nothing was ever stored."
